{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Dartmour: Demo I \u2013 The Barrier at Belstone</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">A faint hum. A scorched ritual circle. And a village, utterly still. <br>You awaken near the silent village of Belstone, its people vanished and its purpose forgotten. Strange forces linger\u2014unseen, but felt.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Dartmour</strong> is a medieval fantasy RPG inspired by <i>Daggerfall</i> and <i>Gothic</i>, focused on eerie exploration, grounded combat, and atmosphere over exposition. This standalone demo offers a short, immersive slice of the full game\u2019s world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\"><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Atmospheric Exploration </strong><br> Traverse the village of Belstone\u2014eerily abandoned, yet marked by signs of recent life. Search ruined homes and overgrown paths for fragments of what came before, and follow quiet clues toward something left unfinished.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Grounded Melee Combat </strong><br> Fight stranded orcs with nothing but a rusted blade. Combat is deliberate and dangerous\u2014every swing drains stamina, and survival means managing your energy carefully.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Resource-Based Recovery </strong><br> Regain stamina by resting near warmth, sleeping in abandoned beds, or finding scraps of food. Limited healing potions offer rare moments of reprieve.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Three Distinct Playstyles </strong><br>Choose from three cultural backgrounds at the start of your journey\u2014each with their own passive bonuses and drawbacks. These shape how you experience the world and handle its dangers</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>A World That Speaks Without Words </strong><br> There are no dialogue trees, XP counters, or quest markers here. The story is told through what you find, what you piece together, and what the world quietly reveals.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> <br>This demo is not a showcase of features\u2014it\u2019s an invitation into the atmosphere and tone of <i>Dartmour</i>. </p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3753290?t=1749041861","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3753290/3cf2d2f1c41e926c165c7c41ddad488bb8557674/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1749041861","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3753290/8f01317b55f1bd181db5b6a4f78a123e4ea40cb9/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1749041861","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3753290/8f01317b55f1bd181db5b6a4f78a123e4ea40cb9/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1749041861","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Game demo","id":10}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[1,5],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Dartmour: Demo I \u2013 The Barrier at Belstone</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">A faint hum. A scorched ritual circle. And a village, utterly still. <br>You awaken near the silent village of Belstone, its people vanished and its purpose forgotten. Strange forces linger\u2014unseen, but felt.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Dartmour</strong> is a medieval fantasy RPG inspired by <i>Daggerfall</i> and <i>Gothic</i>, focused on eerie exploration, grounded combat, and atmosphere over exposition. This standalone demo offers a short, immersive slice of the full game\u2019s world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\"><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Atmospheric Exploration </strong><br> Traverse the village of Belstone\u2014eerily abandoned, yet marked by signs of recent life. Search ruined homes and overgrown paths for fragments of what came before, and follow quiet clues toward something left unfinished.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Grounded Melee Combat </strong><br> Fight stranded orcs with nothing but a rusted blade. Combat is deliberate and dangerous\u2014every swing drains stamina, and survival means managing your energy carefully.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Resource-Based Recovery </strong><br> Regain stamina by resting near warmth, sleeping in abandoned beds, or finding scraps of food. Limited healing potions offer rare moments of reprieve.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Three Distinct Playstyles </strong><br>Choose from three cultural backgrounds at the start of your journey\u2014each with their own passive bonuses and drawbacks. These shape how you experience the world and handle its dangers</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>A World That Speaks Without Words </strong><br> There are no dialogue trees, XP counters, or quest markers here. The story is told through what you find, what you piece together, and what the world quietly reveals.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> <br>This demo is not a showcase of features\u2014it\u2019s an invitation into the atmosphere and tone of <i>Dartmour</i>. </p>","developers":["Runemythic Games"],"fullgame":{"appid":"3752140","name":"Dartmour: Tablets of the Ancients"},"genres":[{"description":"Action","id":"1"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"RPG","id":"3"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3753290/b76b500eddc184eb2d7a5e43254d1b5c23d118f7/header.jpg?t=1749041861","is_free":true,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"highlight":true,"id":257144219,"mp4":{"480":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257144219/movie480.mp4?t=1749041859","max":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257144219/movie_max.mp4?t=1749041859"},"name":"Dartmour Trailer1","thumbnail":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/257144219/f7e7ca055d8bd0e57fac909547d9e901a1ad59ab/